<%- include("../partials/header", { pageTitle: lesson.title + " | LearnFlow AI" }) %>

<main class="learning-page">
    <div class="learning-container lesson-container">
        <header class="learning-topbar">
            <a href="/learning" class="learning-back">← Learning</a>
            <strong class="learning-brand">LearnFlow AI</strong>
        </header>

        <article class="lesson-content">
            <span class="onboarding-step-label">LESSON 01</span>
            <h1><%= lesson.title %></h1>
            <div class="lesson-meta"><span><%= lesson.duration %></span><span>FOUNDATIONS</span></div>

            <p class="lesson-lead"><%= lesson.objective %></p>

            <section class="lesson-section">
                <h2>What is HTML?</h2>
                <p>HTML, or HyperText Markup Language, describes the structure of a webpage. It uses elements such as headings, paragraphs, links, and images to give content meaning.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="lesson-section">
                <h2>Your first HTML document</h2>
                <p>A document usually contains a <code>head</code> for metadata and a <code>body</code> for the content people see.</p>
                <pre><code>&lt;h1&gt;Hello, world!&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My first webpage.&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre>
            </section>

            <div class="lesson-completion">
                <p>Finished this lesson? Check what you learned next.</p>
                <a href="/quiz" class="lesson-action">Mark as Complete <span>→</span></a>
            </div>
        </article>
    </div>
</main>

<%- include("../partials/footer") %>